  "id": "npi",
  "term": "NPI",
  "definition": "NPI refers to the Neuropsychiatric Inventory, a standardized rating scale used to evaluate the severity of neuropsychiatric or behavioral symptoms linked with dementia based on a caregiver’s observations. It covers 12 areas, such as delusions, anxiety, motor changes, and appetite, and rates symptoms only when they are present.",
